      "url": "https://github.com/rox-one/rox-one/pull/1417#discussion_r4173446230",
      "body": "## CodeQL / Unpinned tag for a non-immutable Action or reusable workflow\n\nUnpinned 3rd party Action 'UI-001 Recovery' step [Uses Step](1) uses 'oven-sh/setup-bun' with ref 'v2', not a pinned commit hash\n\n[Show more details](https://github.com/rox-one/rox-one/security/code-scanning/1031)"
    },
    {
      "id": 4173458955,
      "path": "apps/electron/src/renderer/contexts/NavigationContext.tsx",
      "line": 219,
      "commit": "20842365c55889d8dec7b3a164ad7d20df24238b",
      "url": "https://github.com/rox-one/rox-one/pull/1417#discussion_r4173458955",
      "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Enforce workspace mismatch in panel overrides**\n\nWhen a stored/deep-linked session belongs to another workspace, this changes only the `NavigationContext` state to `unavailable`, but the rendered content does not consume that state: `PanelSlot` independently parses `entry.route` and always passes it as `navStateOverride`, and `MainContentPanel` prefers that override over the context value. Consequently, restoring or switching to a workspace while a foreign session route remains selected still mounts `ChatPage` for that session instead of the intended unavailable surface. Apply the workspace check to each panel's parsed state (or ensure the focused panel uses the checked context state).\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
    },
    {
      "id": 4173573441,
      "path": "apps/electron/src/renderer/components/app-shell/MainContentPanel.tsx",
      "line": 244,
      "commit": "20842365c55889d8dec7b3a164ad7d20df24238b",
      "url": "https://github.com/rox-one/rox-one/pull/1417#discussion_r4173573441",
      "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Block foreign chats when metadata is absent**\n\nWhen a workspace switch retains the previous panel route, this check only rejects it if `selectedSession` exists. Fresh evidence in the current code is that `handleSelectWorkspace` explicitly clears `sessionMetaMapAtom` in `App.tsx:2203-2206` before `NavigationContext` reconciles the panels, so the old route renders `ChatPage` with an undefined lookup and can start loading that foreign session during the intervening render. Treat unresolved session metadata as pending/unavailable during a workspace transition rather than allowing it through.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
    },
    {
      "id": 4173573444,
      "path": "apps/electron/src/renderer/contexts/NavigationContext.tsx",
      "line": null,
      "commit": "ec04d7401abe6f7c39ac18526c69a0e448b009bc",
      "url": "https://github.com/rox-one/rox-one/pull/1417#discussion_r4173573444",
      "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Release history suppression when workspace lookup fails**\n\nIf Back/Forward reaches an entry for a workspace that has since been deleted, `handleSwitchWorkspaceBySlug` in `App.tsx:2216-2221` finds no target and returns without changing `workspaceSlug`. No workspace-switch effect then runs to call `finishHistoryReconcile`, leaving both `suppressPushRef` and `isPopstateSwitchRef` set indefinitely; subsequent navigation stops creating history entries and a later UI workspace switch can be mistaken for that stale popstate. Only enter suppression after confirming the switch, or provide a failure path that clears these flags.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
    },
    {
      "id": 4173657621,
