      "commit": "20842365c55889d8dec7b3a164ad7d20df24238b",
      "url": "https://github.com/rox-one/rox-one/pull/1417#discussion_r4173657621",
      "body": "During a workspace switch\\, the workspace\\-mismatch guard fails to block a retained session route whose metadata was just cleared\\, letting ChatPage mount and load the previous workspace\\'s session\\.\n\n<!-- VADE-CATEGORY: concurrency -->\n<!-- VADE-GITHUB-SUGGESTION-ID:94cd160bc0d227b85c12f0e65a69074c5b9c76c86b326b34ad5bf4d287c95e4c -->\n\n<!-- VADE-RECOMMENDATION: FIX -->\n<a href=\"https://vercel.com/0xdx/~/agent/tasks/364a5fae-963b-4c42-9df7-87db846a67a9#suggestion-94cd160bc0d227b85c12f0e65a69074c5b9c76c86b326b34ad5bf4d287c95e4c\" rel=\"noreferrer\"><picture>\n    <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://vercel.com/vercel-agent-view-suggestion-dark\">\n    <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://vercel.com/vercel-agent-view-suggestion-light\">\n    <img src=\"https://vercel.com/vercel-agent-view-suggestion-light\" alt=\"Fix on Vercel\" width=\"127\" height=\"28\" />\n  </picture></a>\n\n<!-- VADE-OUTCOME: ISSUE_RESOLVED -->"
    },
    {
      "id": 4173657624,
      "path": "apps/electron/src/renderer/contexts/NavigationContext.tsx",
      "line": 973,
      "commit": "20842365c55889d8dec7b3a164ad7d20df24238b",
      "url": "https://github.com/rox-one/rox-one/pull/1417#discussion_r4173657624",
      "body": "In the popstate handler\\, `suppressPushRef`\\/`isPopstateSwitchRef` are set to `true` before confirming the target workspace exists\\, so a slug for a deleted\\/unknown workspace leaves both flags stuck at true forever\\, silently disabling history pushes\\.\n\n<!-- VADE-CATEGORY: logic -->\n<!-- VADE-GITHUB-SUGGESTION-ID:369cf6e52d96410cfbbce98e1e67cf7b0cafa385809a1b9e3b4aca97adf08952 -->\n\n<!-- VADE-RECOMMENDATION: FIX -->\n<a href=\"https://vercel.com/0xdx/~/agent/tasks/364a5fae-963b-4c42-9df7-87db846a67a9#suggestion-369cf6e52d96410cfbbce98e1e67cf7b0cafa385809a1b9e3b4aca97adf08952\" rel=\"noreferrer\"><picture>\n    <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://vercel.com/vercel-agent-view-suggestion-dark\">\n    <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://vercel.com/vercel-agent-view-suggestion-light\">\n    <img src=\"https://vercel.com/vercel-agent-view-suggestion-light\" alt=\"Fix on Vercel\" width=\"127\" height=\"28\" />\n  </picture></a>\n\n<!-- VADE-OUTCOME: ISSUE_RESOLVED -->"
    },
    {
      "id": 4173820816,
      "path": ".github/workflows/ui-001-recovery.yml",
      "line": 55,
      "commit": "20842365c55889d8dec7b3a164ad7d20df24238b",
      "url": "https://github.com/rox-one/rox-one/pull/1417#discussion_r4173820816",
      "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Fail CI when committed source hashes diverge**\n\nThis comparison is only written to the receipt and never asserted, so the recovery job remains green even when it tests a different candidate than the committed manifest. That occurs in this commit: for example, the manifest records `303be05d...` for `MainContentPanel.tsx`, while the committed file hashes to `6a49e0bb...` (and several other listed files also differ). Make this step exit nonzero on a mismatch, or update the manifest, so uploaded qualification evidence cannot silently describe an unpinned source set.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
    },
    {
      "id": 4173820818,
      "path": "apps/electron/src/shared/route-parser.ts",
      "line": 949,
      "commit": "20842365c55889d8dec7b3a164ad7d20df24238b",
      "url": "https://github.com/rox-one/rox-one/pull/1417#discussion_r4173820818",
      "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Escape preserved routes in split-panel history**\n\nWhen a malformed known-prefix route containing a comma, such as `knowledge/unknown,id/x`, is opened with `newPanel`, this new fallback preserves the route verbatim. `syncUrl` then concatenates panel routes with commas, while `reconcileFromUrlParams` restores them with `panelsParam.split(',')`, so reload or Back/Forward turns this one route into multiple panels and loses the original address. Encode each panel route independently or use a structured serialization before allowing arbitrary unavailable routes into the panel stack.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
    }
  ]
